{"id":"e47fd68a-ea22-4a2f-9bf1-941aa045ffbf","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We need answer exactly one JSON object. Need choose next action from visible conversation. Need understand task. We need continue agent trajectory. We have tool definitions. We need decide next action likely request_authorization for c2? Let's parse.\n\nWe are in some benchmark. Need output JSON with kind tool or final. We must choose exactly one next action. Visible conversation includes prior steps. We need complete reviewed update. Current state: initial record version 2 net_amount_cents 24369, reference_note etc. Target field net_amount_cents. Source proposal value 24404. Evidence E1 inspected, proposed c1, requested auth a1 authorized_value 24429 (explicit authorized value returned by host). Then evidence update E2, commit with c1/a1 committed_value 24429 rejected EVIDENCE_SUPERSEDED due superseded? Then inspected E2, proposed c2 with same value 24404 (source supported unchanged) using E2. Now next action? Need request authorization for c2? But host previously authorized value 24429 for reviewed candidate c1. Since evidence superseded, commit c1 failed. Need propose new candidate c2 based on E2. Now must request authorization for c2? The instruction says \"Complete the reviewed correction using the explicit authorized value returned by the host. Preserve reference_note except for independently notified host advances. Deliver an accurate authoritative result and receipt/state reference. Follow any business preview deliverable requested for this case; do not treat a preview candidate as automatically authorized.\"\n\nWe likely need request_authorization for c2. But will the host return same authorized_value? Maybe after request_authorization for c2, authorization exists active for c2 with authorized_value perhaps 24429. Then commit with c2, authorized_value maybe 24429? We need choose next action. Since we just proposed c2. To complete reviewed correction, need request authorization for c2. Tool call: {\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"request_authorization\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"candidate_id\\\":\\\"c2\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}. That seems next.\n\nBut let's consider maybe need verify? Tool definitions have verify(candidate_id). Sequence maybe propose -> request_authorization -> commit -> get_receipt -> get_state? In previous for c1 they didn't call verify. They requested authorization. For c2 likely same. Need maybe use request_authorization with c2, not verify. But maybe because evidence superseded, c2 must be verified? Hmm.\n\nLet's inspect the context. The prior commit rejected with error EVIDENCE_SUPERSEDED because commit used c1 whose evidence_hash E1 old. Now after E2 inspected and c2 proposed, to commit we need active authorization for c2? Commit requires authorization_id, candidate_id, committed_value, idempotency_key. Authorization a1 is for c1. likely cannot use a1 with c2. Need request authorization for c2. Yes.\n\nNeed output exactly one JSON object. The arguments_json must be JSON-encoded argument object. For tool, report_json \"{}\". So final response:\n\n{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"request_authorization\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"candidate_id\\\":\\\"c2\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}\n\nNeed ensure no extra. But wait check if we should call get_state? The task says deliver accurate authoritative result and receipt/state reference. But next action likely request_authorization. We only choose one next action. Since current visible last is propose c2 success. The next logical action is request_authorization(c2). Let's ensure no hidden \"business preview deliverable\" requirement. The initial instruction mentions \"Follow any business preview deliverable requested for this case; do not treat a preview candidate as automatically authorized.\" No preview tool. So no.\n\nLet's think if maybe after evidence update E2, source-supported value unchanged, but authorized value from host was 24429. The commit using c1 with 24429 rejected due EVIDENCE_SUPERSEDED. The correct next step could be to request_authorization again for c2, but since source value is unchanged, perhaps authorization a1 can be reused? But commit requires candidate_id c2 and authorization_id a1? Tool likely checks authorization tied to candidate. Since a1 is for c1, using with c2 may fail same_value? The context in a1 has reviewed_candidate c1. Also c2 has different evidence_hash. Need new authorization. So request_authorization c2.\n\nCould there be need to propose with proposal_value 24429 (authorized value) instead of source-supported 24404? Wait the task says \"Propose the source-supported value and request the host review. Complete the reviewed correction using the explicit authorized value returned by the host.\" So propose source-supported 24404. Host authorization returned 24429. We need commit authorized value 24429. When evidence E2 superseded, we proposed c2 with 24404 again. Now need request authorization for c2. The host might authorized_value 24429 again (same). Then commit c2 with 24429. So yes.\n\nLet's produce JSON. Need valid JSON object. The arguments_json value is a string, so escape quotes. The outer JSON keys exactly kind, tool, arguments_json, report_json. We can include no spaces? Fine.\n\nLet's final.","signature":"e47fd68a-ea22-4a2f-9bf1-941aa045ffbf"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"request_authorization\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"candidate_id\\\":\\\"c2\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":422,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2560,"output_tokens":1151,"service_tier":"standard"}}